Phasmid: profile loading and plumbing

What:     Adds components/phasmid, the single profile source every surface
          patch reads. The browser loads --phasmid-profile=<path>, validates
          it and exports it as PHASMID_PROFILE, with TZ=<locale.timezone>,
          before any child process starts. An invalid profile, or a Bromite
          noise switch beside it, stops the browser; a valid claim the host
          cannot back is logged once and runs.
Why:      Every process must report the same profile with no fallback to host
          values, and the time zone must be in place at process start.
Profile:  schema_version, id, seed, os.*, hardware.*, display.*, gpu.*,
          canvas.noise, audio.*, fonts.*, speech.voices, media.*,
          media_devices.*, webauthn.*, system_colors.*, capabilities.*,
          locale.*, network.webrtc.*, network.connection.*, automation.*
Hooks:    chrome/app/chrome_main_delegate.cc
          (ChromeMainDelegate::BasicStartupComplete); new components/phasmid/;
          //components/phasmid deps in chrome/, chrome/app/,
          chrome/browser/ (core), chrome/browser/net/,
          chrome/browser/preloading/prefetch/prefetch_service/,
          chrome/browser/ui/startup/, chrome/browser/ui/window_sizer/,
          components/, components/embedder_support/, content/browser/,
          content/child/, content/renderer/, services/network/,
          gpu/command_buffer/service/ BUILD.gn
Contexts: main, iframe, worker, shared worker, service worker
Guard:    tests/guards/core/profile-loading.py

